cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Reqover: request-level runtime coverage attribution for Spring MVC and WebFlux"
message: "If you use Reqover in academic work, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: TaeHui
    alias: TaeHuiKKIM
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Sangmin
    alias: lsmin3388
repository-code: "https://github.com/reqover-labs/reqover"
url: "https://github.com/reqover-labs/reqover"
abstract: >-
  Reqover attributes runtime coverage to the HTTP request that produced it. A
  Java agent inserts method-entry probes, per-request buckets keep concurrent
  requests separate, and Reactor context propagation preserves attribution
  across WebFlux thread hops. The resulting endpoint-to-code and
  code-to-endpoint indexes are exported as JSON so a CI job can turn a diff
  into the list of endpoints to retest.
keywords:
  - code-coverage
  - java-agent
  - bytecode-instrumentation
  - spring-boot
  - webflux
  - test-impact-analysis
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-21"
